     "text": "{\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Check UT-AIR telemetry for header_pressure_bar and compressor_current_a leading up to the stop: continuous high current with depressed header pressure supports a major plant-wide air demand or compressor mechanical fault, whereas normal pressure and cycling refute a central utility supply problem.\",\n    \"Check ST20-WLD telemetry for air_pressure_bar around 2026-09-19T21:32:59Z: pressure dropping below the normal range (5.3 to 5.9 bar) supports a localized pneumatic leak or regulator malfunction in Weld cell A, while normal local pressure refutes a pneumatic drop at the station.\",\n    \"Compare ST30-WLD air_pressure_bar against ST20-WLD air_pressure_bar: if ST30-WLD maintains normal pressure while ST20-WLD is low, this refutes a common header drop and isolates the leak or obstruction to the ST20 branch; if both are depressed, it supports a shared utility supply deficiency.\",\n    \"Evaluate ST20-WLD air_pressure_bar for sensor or telemetry failure by checking for signal flatlining, out-of-range ADC counts, or sudden discontinuous drop without corresponding pneumatic behavior: sudden step changes or zero values without mechanical alarm support a faulty pressure transmitter, while smooth dynamic variation refutes a sensor failure.\",\n    \"Check ST20-WLD cycle_time_s and servo_temp_c to observe whether pneumatic clamp actuation delays or weld faults occurred prior to the hold: cycle time expansion supports functional mechanical impairment from inadequate air pressure, whereas nominal cycle times refute acute mechanical stalling before the manual hold.\"\n  ],\n  \"upstream_step\": 0,\n  \"sensor_step\": 3,\n  \"suspects\": [\n    \"UT-AIR\",\n    \"ST20-WLD\",\n    \"ST30-WLD\"\n  ]\n} "
